{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_galedra", "label": "Galedra", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://galedra.org", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An epistemic ledger exists because AI research is expensive to repeat and hard to audit; a durable, signed, reusable evidence record makes that work cumulative. It is deliberately not a source of truth but a source of traceable reasons for believing or doubting a claim."}, {"id": "readme_galeed", "label": "Galeed (Genesis 31:47-48) naming origin", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The cairn Jacob and Laban piled up: two parties, no shared authority, a durable marker left in the open. The name was chosen because the same shape applies to claims rather than covenants."}, {"id": "readme_epistemic_ledger", "label": "Epistemic Ledger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_contribution_log", "label": "Signed hash-chained contribution log", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The log is the source of record so that dropping every projection table and replaying returns identical snapshot hashes and scores; gap-free sequence numbers make a snapshot addressable without trusting a timestamp."}, {"id": "readme_projections", "label": "Projections are replayable", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_evidence_vs_conclusions", "label": "Evidence and conclusions are different objects", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A passage is evidence; 'this passage supports X' is a separate, attributable link, so each can be challenged independently instead of collapsing interpretation into the source."}, {"id": "readme_contradictions_coexist", "label": "Contradictions coexist", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_deterministic_scoring", "label": "Deterministic, versioned, replaceable scoring", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same snapshot plus same model version yields a byte-identical result, down to a recomputable trace. Two models ship so they can be compared on the same graph; the UI reports '0.86 under ledger-default@0.1.0 at snapshot 212' to prevent a number reading as truth."}, {"id": "readme_confidence_is_not_coverage", "label": "Confidence is not coverage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_insufficient_evidence", "label": "Unknown is a first-class result (INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A claim with no counted evidence must report INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE rather than falling back to the prior, because a prior-derived direction would manufacture a verdict from nothing."}, {"id": "readme_independence_groups", "label": "Repetition is not corroboration (independence groups)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Evidence sharing an upstream origin is grouped and only the strongest member counts, so four citations tracing to one survey of 400 people cannot look like four corroborations."}, {"id": "readme_agents_are_contributors", "label": "Agents are contributors, not arbiters", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An agent leases a signed task packet with the smallest sufficient context and returns a signed result validated server-side. Reputation tracks audited reliability at specific tasks in specific domains and deliberately does not enter claim scores in v0.1, so it can never become authority."}, {"id": "readme_determinism_is_not_objectivity", "label": "Determinism is not objectivity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Relevance labels, interpretive steps, independence groupings and claim wording are judgments; making them explicit, attributed, challengeable and versioned is honest, pretending they are objective is not."}, {"id": "readme_record_investigation", "label": "record_investigation: one call records the whole check", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_mcp_connect", "label": "Connected assistants over MCP and OAuth", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_demo", "label": "bin/demo golden-value demo and replay check", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}